  "summary": "A dragged block lands wherever the compiled schema accepts it, at any depth: landAt in packages/plitejs/src/core/landing.ts runs one per-edge law (identity, a redirect-only landing read, canPlaceAt placement, every transferVeto) for drags, keyboard steps, file drops and editor.api.transfer. Column, Table, Details and Footnote keep their limits as vetoes, List redirects only, and Upload replaces only an empty block-content block. The hover walk in dom-drag.ts hit-tests the level's center line, falls back to a mounted binary search that skips coverage-unmounted ranges, bands container edges and refuses collapsed edges through the coverage index. editor.read.transfer.nodes replaces editor.read.transfer.source; a keyboard step across parents refuses. The copied dnd.tsx gives every selectable block-content element a handle, shows only the innermost hovered one and no longer hides handles for a selected table. Docs, Best API teaching, doctrine v257, vision, editor-behavior law and changesets match. The planned empty collapsed range for a summary-only details was reverted because coverage has no empty range.",
